* Lab 19-11: a 1 mm routed net on SKY130 metal 1 (Example 19-11.6a and its sanity check)
* Driver: SKY130 inv_1's pull-up as a linear resistor R_eq = 5.64 kohm / ln 2 = 8136.8 ohm from an ideal step.
* (5.64 kohm is the Liberty delay slope, which already contains ln 2; the physical resistor is R_eff / ln 2.)
* Wire: the open flow's metal-1 estimate, 1.20565 ohm/um and 0.172375 fF/um, as a 40-section pi ladder
* (whose Elmore delay equals the continuous wire's). Load: inv_1's input, 2.302 fF.
* Elmore constant = area above the unit-step response; t50 = 50% crossing.
* EXPECT elmore key:README.md#Lab_19-11.g scale=1e-12 rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT t50 key:README.md#Lab_19-11.f scale=1e-12 rtol=2e-3
Vin in 0 PWL(0 0 1f 1)
Rd in n0 8136.8
Rw0 n0 n1 30.14125
Rw1 n1 n2 30.14125
Rw2 n2 n3 30.14125
Rw3 n3 n4 30.14125
Rw4 n4 n5 30.14125
Rw5 n5 n6 30.14125
Rw6 n6 n7 30.14125
Rw7 n7 n8 30.14125
